+<H2>
+<FONT SIZE="-1">
+javax.annotation</FONT>
+<BR>
+Annotation Type CheckForSigned</H2>
+<HR>
+<DL>
+<DT><PRE><FONT SIZE="-1">@Documented
+<A HREF="../../javax/annotation/meta/TypeQualifierNickname.html" title="annotation in javax.annotation.meta">@TypeQualifierNickname</A>
+<A HREF="../../javax/annotation/Nonnegative.html" title="annotation in javax.annotation">@Nonnegative</A>(<A HREF="../../javax/annotation/Nonnegative.html#when()">when</A>=<A HREF="../../javax/annotation/meta/When.html#MAYBE">MAYBE</A>)
+@Retention(value=RUNTIME)
+</FONT>public @interface <B>CheckForSigned</B></DL>
+</PRE>
+
+<P>
+Used to annotate a value that may be either negative or nonnegative, and
+ indicates that uses of it should check for
+ negative values before using it in a way that requires the value to be
+ nonnegative, and check for it being nonnegative before using it in a way that
+ requires it to be negative.
+<P>
